sequenceDiagram
    participant User       as User
    participant Browser    as Web Browser
    participant Hub        as JupyterHub
    participant Proxy      as JupyterHub Proxy
    participant IdP        as ESCAPE SSO (IdP) iam-escape.cloud.cnaf.infn.it
    participant JLab       as JupyterLab Pod
    participant Ext        as REANA JupyterLab Extension
    participant RServer    as REANA Server
    participant DB         as REANA Database
    participant K8s        as Kubernetes Cluster

%% ── Login to JupyterLab ─────────────────────────────────────────────
    User    ->> Browser : Press "Sign in with OAuth 2.0"

    Browser ->> Hub     : GET /oauth_login
    Hub     ->> Browser : 302 Redirect → ESCAPE SSO: /authorize?<PARAMS>

    Browser ->> IdP     : GET /authorize?<PARAMS> (OIDC request)
    IdP     ->> Browser : 302 Redirect → ESCAPE SSO: /login

    Browser ->> IdP     : GET /login
%% ── ^^^^^^ Where is the connection between session and return url? JSESSIONID is specific to login session? How does the sso known where to return?
    IdP     ->> Browser : ESCAPE HTML Login Form

    Browser ->> User     : Display Login Form
    User    ->> Browser  : Enter credentials and submit
%% ── I am here ─────────────────────────────────────────────
%% Now the user gets redirected multiple times somehow, go through this now!
    Browser ->> Hub     : /oauth_callback?code=…
    Hub     ->> IdP     : Exchange code for tokens
    IdP     ->> Hub     : ID & Access tokens
    Hub     ->> Hub     : Validate tokens & identify user
    Hub     ->> K8s     : Spawn JupyterLab pod (namespace+PVC)
    K8s     ->> Hub     : Pod ready
    Hub     ->> Proxy   : Register route /user/{user}/
    Hub     ->> Browser : 302 → /user/{user}/lab
    Browser ->> Proxy   : GET /user/{user}/lab (with session cookie)
    Proxy   ->> JLab    : Forward request
    JLab    ->> Proxy   : JupyterLab UI HTML/JS
    Proxy   ->> Browser : Serve JupyterLab UI

%% ── REANA extension initialisation ─────────────────────────────────
    User    ->> Ext     : Enter REANA URL + token
    Ext     ->> Ext     : Store token (localStorage)
    Ext     ->> RServer : GET /api/workflows (Bearer token)
    RServer ->> DB      : Validate token
    DB      ->> RServer : User record
    RServer ->> Ext     : Workflow list
    RServer -->> Ext    : 401 Unauthorized %% if token invalid

%% ── Launch workflow ────────────────────────────────────────────────
    User    ->> Ext     : Create workflow
    Ext     ->> RServer : POST /api/workflows
    RServer ->> DB      : Authorise action
    RServer ->> K8s     : Create workflow jobs
    K8s     ->> RServer : Jobs running
    RServer ->> Ext     : Workflow ID & status
    Ext     ->> RServer : Poll status/logs
    RServer ->> Ext     : Current status

%% Session persists until logout/expiry
